%T A399450 61,0,1,0,1,0,1,640,0,0,13,2,0,1,67,1163,960,821,1,55,4,1,0,1,32,0,
%U A399450 8192,1,648,1,256,27,0,0,1,1,6883,17152,41261,15,9031,256,153,1,1,0
%N A399450 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) = (1/n) * Sum_{x in (Z_n)^k} exp(2*Pi*i*det(circ(x))/n).
%C A399450 Here, the summation is over all vectors x of length k with values in Z_n and det(circ(x)) is the determinant of the circulant matrix whose first row is x.
%C A399450 All columns are multiplicative.
%H A399450 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A399450/b399450.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..120</a> (first 15 antidiagonals).
%H A399450 Zoltan Reti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21969894">The Multiple Gauss Sums Behind A007789-A007792</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A399450 Zoltan Reti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21970261">Multiple Gauss Sums Generated by Circulant Matrices</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A399450 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circulant_matrix">Circulant matrix</a>.
%e A399450 Array begins:
